section.section:
    validateRequest()
validateRequestCsrf
CsrfvalidateRequest

validateRequest ( $removeAfterValidation = false
)[static]

Validates a CSRF token from the request (POST or GET). Checks $_POST['csrf_token'] first, then $_GET['csrf_token'], then headers.





Parameters










bool$removeAfterValidation

Whether to remove the token after successful validation 







                Returns


bool True if token is valid, false otherwise 




Definition at line 186 of file class.csrf.php.
00187     {
00188         // Check POST first (most common for AJAX)
00189         if (isset($_POST['csrf_token'])) {
00190             return self::validateToken($_POST['csrf_token'], $removeAfterValidation);
00191         }
00192 
00193         // Check GET as fallback
00194         if (isset($_GET['csrf_token'])) {
00195             return self::validateToken($_GET['csrf_token'], $removeAfterValidation);
00196         }
00197 
00198         // Check custom header (for AJAX requests)
00199         $headers = self::getAllHeaders();
00200 
00201         // Check for X-CSRF-Token header (case-insensitive)
00202         foreach ($headers as $key => $value) {
00203             if (strtolower($key) === 'x-csrf-token') {
00204                 return self::validateToken($value, $removeAfterValidation);
00205             }
00206         }
00207 
00208         Log::warning('CSRF validation failed: No token in request');
00209         return false;
